From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:41:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Run the PEG equalization of the W541 OEM
 firmware

The OEM firmware of the ThinkPad W541 (GNET94WW) programs the 8 GT/s
presets of its NVIDIA GPU link with preset 3 for the root port, 7 for
the GPU and receiver preset hint 2, in the System Agent policy its
CpuInitPhnxPei module builds, then runs the 8 GT/s equalization of the
reference code; the Gen3 preset search of that code is off in its
setup data (SaPpiSetupVar). Give the W541 those presets in its
devicetree, and the setup option peg_link_tuning its new value, "As the
Lenovo firmware", the default: Intel's AFE settings, the presets and the
equalization.

The T440p keeps Intel's presets, which its OEM firmware uses.

TEST=Built for Lenovo ThinkPad W541, mrc.bin and native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c                     | 10 ++++++----
 .../lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb         |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index d40f965a68..e81dcf7130 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -497,15 +497,17 @@ static const struct sm_object peg_link_tuning = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 			  0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
 	.opt_name	= "peg_link_tuning",
 	.ui_name	= "NVIDIA GPU link tuning",
-	.ui_helptext	= "Settings of the PCIe link to the NVIDIA GPU, programmed\n"
-			  "before it trains: Intel's analog front-end (AFE) settings,\n"
-			  "and Intel's transmitter presets for 8 GT/s (PCIe 3.0).\n"
-			  "Off: the hardware defaults. Takes effect at the next boot.",
+	.ui_helptext	= "Settings of the PCIe link to the NVIDIA GPU: Intel's analog\n"
+			  "front-end (AFE) settings and the transmitter presets for\n"
+			  "8 GT/s (PCIe 3.0) before the link trains, then the 8 GT/s\n"
+			  "equalization of the Lenovo firmware. Off: the hardware\n"
+			  "defaults. Takes effect at the next boot.",
 	.default_value	= PEG_TUNING_DEFAULT,
 	.values		= (const struct sm_enum_value[]) {
 				{ "Off",			PEG_TUNING_OFF		},
 				{ "AFE",			PEG_TUNING_AFE		},
 				{ "AFE and 8 GT/s presets",	PEG_TUNING_AFE_PRESETS	},
+				{ "As the Lenovo firmware",	PEG_TUNING_EQUALIZATION	},
 				SM_ENUM_VALUE_END					},
 }, WITH_DEP_VALUES(&enable_dual_graphics, true));
 
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb
index 6f218144ea..14b2f4fa4d 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb
@@ -14,6 +14,13 @@ chip northbridge/intel/haswell
 	}"
 	register "ec_present" = "true"
 	register "spd_addresses" = "{0x50, 0x52, 0x51, 0x53}"
+	# The 8 GT/s presets of the OEM firmware (GNET94WW) for the NVIDIA GPU
+	register "peg_cfg[0]" = "{
+		.gen3_presets	= true,
+		.gen3_rp_preset	= 3,
+		.gen3_ep_preset	= 7,
+		.gen3_ep_hint	= 2,
+	}"
 	chip cpu/intel/haswell
 		device cpu_cluster 0 on ops haswell_cpu_bus_ops end
 	end
